1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,270
If this parasite gets inside a snail,

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:03,325
it can turn its eyes

3
00:00:03,365 --> 00:00:05,090
into moving bait.

4
00:00:05,130 --> 00:00:06,470
The worm grows through its body

5
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:07,750
and fills its eyestalks

6
00:00:07,790 --> 00:00:09,940
with pulsing, colorful sacs.

7
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:10,765
They start looking like

8
00:00:10,805 --> 00:00:12,490
tiny caterpillars.

9
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:15,140
And that's exactly what the parasite wants.

10
00:00:15,180 --> 00:00:16,465
Because when a bird spots one

11
00:00:16,505 --> 00:00:17,260
and eats it,

12
00:00:17,300 --> 00:00:19,810
the parasite gets inside the bird.

13
00:00:19,850 --> 00:00:21,115
Then its eggs spread

14
00:00:21,155 --> 00:00:22,600
through the bird's droppings,

15
00:00:22,640 --> 00:00:24,560
ready to infect another snail.

